# AST span rows that every engine reads conformantly, so no engine will ever
# close them. Read by scripts/declaration-audit.mjs, which otherwise requires
# resources/ast-span-divergence.txt and its measurement twin LAST_MEASURED in
# tests/ast-spans.test.mjs to be EMPTY before a tag. One line covers both,
# because they record one fact from two sides. There are no such rows now.
#
# One per line, `<type> (presence|extent)@<count>: <reason>`, in the shape
# .fleet-pin-exempt uses. The reason is required and must name what makes the
# readings conformant, either a fully qualified `owner/repo#N` or a
# `CARVE-Pnn-nnn` clause id. A bare key, an empty reason, and a reason naming
# neither are errors rather than skips, so a line here cannot degrade into a
# blanket pass. Every declaration that applies is printed on a passing run.
#
# THE COUNT IS PART OF THE KEY, for the reason .fleet-pin-exempt keys on the
# pin's sha. A line naming only the type outlives the reading it describes and
# silences the next one; keyed on the document count it stops applying the
# moment the divergence spreads or shrinks, and the audit says so rather than
# passing. A line whose type no longer diverges at all is an error telling you
# to delete it.
#
# WHAT DOES NOT BELONG HERE is a row an engine owes. The list and item rows
# became owed under markup-carve/carve#5063: leading indentation belongs to
# their spans at the owner's content column. They remain in the span ledger
# until the engines move.
